oals with the two planetary encounters, mission planners directed the veteran spacecraft to Uranus\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The spacecraft directed to Uranus is Voyager 2, not Voyager 3.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-003\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"Although Voyager 2 had fulfilled its primary mission goals with the two planetary encounters, mission planners directed the veteran spacecraft to Uranus—a journey that would take about 4,5 years\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The journey duration matches but the spacecraft is Voyager 2, not Voyager 3.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-004\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"Although Voyager 2 had fulfilled its primary mission goals with the two planetary encounters\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The Jupiter encounter optimization is stated for Voyager 2, so the name Voyager 3 is incompatible.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-005\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"The Uranus encounter’s geometry was also defined by the possibility of a future encounter with Neptune\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference says the future encounter was with Neptune, not Saturn.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-006\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"Voyager 2 had only 5.5 hours of close study during its flyby\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference gives Voyager 2 and 5.5 hours, not Voyager 1 and 6.4 days.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-007\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"The first human-made object to fly past Uranus, Voyager 2's long-range observations\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference identifies Voyager 2, not Voyager 1, as the first human-made object to fly past Uranus.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-008\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"Voyager 2's long-range observations of the planet began Nov. 4, 1985\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference states Voyager 2's long-range observations began Nov. 4, 1985, which differs in spacecraft, range type and date.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-009\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"Voyager 2's long-range observations of the planet began Nov. 4, 1985, when signals took approximately 2,5 hours to reach Earth\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The signal time matches but the reference attributes it to Voyager 2's long-range observations, not Voyager 1's short-range ones.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-010\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"Light conditions were 400 times less than terrestrial conditions\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference gives 400 times, not five hundred times.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-011\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"Closest approach to Uranus took place at 17:59 UT Jan. 24, 1986\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference gives UT and the year 1986, not ED and 1968.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-012\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"at a range of about 50,640 miles (81,500 kilometers)\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference gives 50,640 miles and 81,500 kilometers, so the claim swaps the units.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-001\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"During its flyby, Voyager 2 discovered 10 new moons\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference states 10 new moons, not 11.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-002\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"given such names as Puck, Portia, Juliet, Cressida, Rosalind, Belinda, Desdemona, Cordelia, Ophelia, and Bianca\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Several of the names in the claim differ from those given in the reference, such as Puck, Portia, Juliet and Cordelia.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-003\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"obvious allusions to Shakespeare\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference says the names allude to Shakespeare, not Goethe.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-004\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"continuing a naming tradition begun in 1787\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference dates the naming tradition to 1787, not 1687.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-005\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"two new rings in addition to the “older” nine rings\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference states two new rings, not three.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-006\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"two new rings in addition to the “older” nine rings\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference states nine previously known rings, not eight.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-007\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"a magnetic field tilted at 59 degrees off-axis and off-center\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference gives a tilt of 59 degrees, not 66 degrees.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-008\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"a magnetic field tilted at 59 degrees off-axis and off-center\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference states the magnetic field discovered by Voyager 2 is off-center.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-009\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"wind speeds in Uranus’ atmosphere as high as 450 miles per hour (724 kilometers per hour)\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference gives 450 miles per hour (724 km/h), not 450 km/h or 72400 meters per hour.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-010\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"found evidence of a boiling ocean of water some 497 miles (800 kilometers) below the top cloud surface\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference states a boiling ocean at 497 miles (800 kilometers), not a lake at 479 miles (900 kilometers).\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-011\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Its rings were found to be extremely variable in thickness and transparency\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference states this directly about the rings of Uranus.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-012\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"Voyager 2 also returned spectacular photos of Miranda, Oberon, Ariel, Umbriel, and Titania\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference names Ariel, Umbriel and Titania, not Ariele, Umbrella and Titan.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-013\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"Miranda, Oberon, Ariel, Umbriel, and Titania, five of Uranus’ larger moons\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference calls them larger moons and gives different names for three of them.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-014\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"In flying by Miranda at a range of only 17.560 miles (28.260 kilometers)\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference gives the same Miranda flyby range in the same figures.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-015\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"the spacecraft came closest to any object so far in its nearly decade-long travels\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference states that the Miranda flyby was the spacecraft's closest approach to any object so far.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-016\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"the spacecraft came closest to any object so far in its nearly decade-long travels\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference describes the travels as nearly decade-long, not nearly century-long.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-017\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Images of the moon showed a strange object whose surface was a mishmash of peculiar features\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference states this about Miranda, referred to as the moon in the sentence following its flyby.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-018\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Uranus itself appeared generally featureless\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference states Uranus appeared generally featureless in the context of Voyager 2's observations.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-019\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"The spectacular news of the Uranus encounter was interrupted the same week by the tragic Challenger accident\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference says the interruption came the same week, not the same day, with the accident four days after closest approach.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-020\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"the tragic Challenger accident that killed seven astronauts\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference states seven astronauts were killed, not six.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-021\",\"verdict\":\"CONTRADICTED\",\"evidence\":\"during their space shuttle launch Jan. 28, 1986\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference dates the launch accident to Jan. 28, 1986, not Feb. 28, 1986.\"}]}","ttft_ms":33673,"type":"result","duration_ms":33692,"uuid":"edf02255-e0e6-426a-b8b7-834cea9e6dd3","ttft_stream_ms":4068,"time_to_request_ms":1877,"first_content_frame_ms":4068,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
